{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranching2Row","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranching2Row","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTDimHLFPair","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranchingRecursion"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimHLF_branching_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimHLF_branching_pair","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranching2Row.lean#L83-L137","doc":"**(A) corner-removal recursion on two rows (sorry-free).**\n`dimHLF [a, b] = branchSum dimHLF [a, b]` for `a ≥ b ≥ 1`: the brute-force hook-length dimension of a\ntwo-row shape equals the sum over removable corners of the dimensions of the corner-removed shapes —\nthe two-row instance of obligation (A) for the general hook-length formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.pascal_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.pascal_sub","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranching2Row.lean#L76-L81","doc":"Pascal's rule in subtraction-normalised form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.choose_mono_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.choose_mono_pair","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranching2Row.lean#L62-L74","doc":"Binomial monotonicity in the lower index up to the centre: `C(n, k−1) ≤ C(n, k)` whenever\n`k ≤ n − k` (here applied with `n − k = a ≥ b = k`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.removableCornerIdxs_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.removableCornerIdxs_pair","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranching2Row.lean#L51-L60","doc":"The removable corners of a two-row shape `[a, b]` with `b ≥ 1`: row `0` iff `b < a`, plus row `1`\nalways. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.decrementRow_pair1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.decrementRow_pair1","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranching2Row.lean#L47-L49","doc":"Decrement the second row of a two-row shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.decrementRow_pair0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.decrementRow_pair0","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranching2Row.lean#L43-L45","doc":"Decrement the first row of a two-row shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimHLF_zero_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimHLF_zero_row","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranching2Row.lean#L36-L41","doc":"`dimHLF [a, 0] = 1` — the empty second row carries the one-row dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.prodHooks_zero_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.prodHooks_zero_row","kind":"theorem","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranching2Row.lean#L23-L34","doc":"`prodHooks [a, 0] = a!` — the hook product of a shape with an empty second row. ","signatureChunk":0}]}